<task id="SRFR-035" project="set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>RegardingResolver auto-refresh v1.3.1 → v1.3.2 (post-selection form refresh, additive to SRFR-034 manual refresh button)</title>
    <status>completed</status>
    <estimated-effort>1h30min</estimated-effort>
    <actual-effort>~50min</actual-effort>
    <assigned>AI Agent</assigned>
    <started>2026-07-03</started>
    <completed>2026-07-03</completed>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-group>—</parallel-group>
    <tags>pcf,regarding-resolver,fluent-ui,react,auto-refresh,version-bump,wave-3-followon,deploy</tags>
    <depends-on>SRFR-034</depends-on>
    <wave>3</wave>
  </metadata>

  <prompt><![CDATA[
Out-of-plan follow-on to SRFR-034 (v1.3.1 deploy). Owner feedback after v1.3.1
UAT on sprk_todo form: "make the PCF auto save and update after record is
selected (i.e. don't force user to hit save or refresh)".

Interpretation: `applyResolverFields` uses `webApi.updateRecord` (writes
committed directly, not staged in form buffer). So the records are ALREADY
saved after selection. What owner wants: after selection completes,
auto-refresh the form display so any form fields bound to
`sprk_regardingrecordnumber` / `sprk_regardingrecordname` / etc. refresh
immediately without user clicking Save/Refresh.

The manual refresh button added in SRFR-034 stays (useful escape hatch) —
auto-refresh is ADDITIVE.

Scope (all in `src/client/pcf/RegardingResolver/`):

1. `RegardingResolverApp.tsx` — after `applyRegardingSelection` completes
   successfully in `handlePickerSelect`, call a new `autoRefreshForm(formType)`
   helper that:
   - Skips on CREATE mode (formType === 1) — presave bridge owns that path
     (SRFR-032 wired the __sprk_regarding_pending__ seam; refreshing during
     CREATE would clobber the buffered attributes)
   - Otherwise calls `formContext.data.entity.save()` (to flush any
     bound-property writes queued in the form buffer) then
     `formContext.data.refresh(true)` to pull server-side updated values
   - Silent-continues on any error (warn only; test-harness safety)
   - Silent-continues if Xrm unavailable

2. Version bump v1.3.1 → v1.3.2 across all 7 anchors per SRFR-033's checklist:
   ControlManifest.Input.xml (2 places — control version attr + potentially
   default-value additions), index.ts CONTROL_VERSION, UI footer BUILD_DATE,
   Solution/solution.xml, Solution Control Manifest,
   package.json, pack.ps1.

3. Add 3 new unit tests to `__tests__/RegardingResolverApp.test.tsx`:
   - UPDATE mode selection (formType === 2) → auto-refresh invoked (save +
     refresh called)
   - CREATE mode selection (formType === 1) → auto-refresh SKIPPED (presave
     path owns it)
   - Xrm unavailable → auto-refresh silent-continues (no throw)

4. Bulk update existing tests: version prop 1.3.1 → 1.3.2 and version regex.

Step 9.5 quality gates: /code-review + /adr-check + `npm run build:prod`.

Deploy: pack solution, `pac solution import --force-overwrite`, verify via
`pac solution list`.

Coordination: SRFR-036 running in parallel (form config for sprk_todo) —
different files, no collision.
  ]]></prompt>

  <role>PCF developer familiar with Spaarke PCF version discipline (`src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md`), Fluent v9 Griffel + tokens (`ADR-021`), virtual PCF platform-library pattern (`ADR-022`), shared PolymorphicPicker (`ADR-012`), and Xrm form-context lifecycle (save + refresh, formType semantics).</role>

  <goal><![CDATA[
RegardingResolver v1.3.2 deployed to spaarkedev1, verified via
`pac solution list`. After successful picker selection in UPDATE mode, form
auto-refreshes so newly-populated fields (bound to sprk_regardingrecordnumber
etc.) display immediately without user Save/Refresh clicks. CREATE mode is
untouched (presave bridge owns it). Manual refresh button from SRFR-034
preserved. All 7 version anchors bumped 1.3.1 → 1.3.2. Tests updated with
3 new auto-refresh coverage tests. `npm run build:prod` passes. ADR-021/
022/012 preserved. Backward compat: existing v1.3.1 form bindings continue
to function; auto-refresh is silent-continue on any Xrm-unavailable path.
  ]]></goal>

